  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\n`#matrix-dev:matrix.org` and `#matrix:matrix.org` both seem in a weird state.\r\n\r\nWhen I try to send a message, I get:\r\n```\r\nUser @kurt:roeckx.be not in room !cURbafjkfsMDVwdRDQ:matrix.org (None)\r\nResend message or cancel message now.\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr:\r\n```\r\nUser @kurt:roeckx.be not in room !XqBunHwQIXUiqCaoxq:matrix.org (None)\r\nResend message or cancel message now.\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen I try to leave the room I get:\r\n```\r\nFailed to leave room\r\nNot a known room\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen I try to join the room I ussually get:\r\n```\r\n\"#matrix:matrix.org is not accessible at this time.\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nSometimes I get:\r\n```\r\nYou are trying to access a room.\r\nClick here to join the discussion!\r\n```\r\nAnd when I then click, I get:\r\n```\r\nFailed to join room\r\nInternal server error\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n<!-- IMPORTANT: please answer the following questions, to help us narrow down the problem -->\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: roeckx.be\r\n\r\nIf not matrix.org:\r\n- **Version**: 0.31.2-1\r\n- **Install method**: .deb pacakge\r\n- **Platform**:  debian stable",
